# THE ATTACHED VOLUME — a bedstee on a cottage wall, a balcony on a tree.
#
# ⚠ ONE PRIMITIVE, TWO PICTURES. A sleeping alcove is NOT cut into a wall: it is a
# wooden box built ONTO it. A balcony is mostly outside its trunk but bites a little
# INTO the round of it, so straight wood has something flat to land on and a door
# can go through what is left. They differ in two numbers and a kind.

echo --- flat ground
at 0 0 0
key ArrowUp
wait rebuilt

echo --- a cottage wall, and a bedstee built against it
at -10 6 0
verb run
at -2 6 0
verb run
at -6 4.2 90
key J

echo --- and a cupboard hard against it: five walls for two boxes, not six
key V

echo --- a bed in the box, sized by the box rather than given a size
select seat 0
verb seat

echo --- a trunk: a ring of wall, which is a cylinder
at 6 6 0
key G
wait rebuilt

echo --- and a balcony on its east side
at 9 6 0
key K

echo --- a niche in the cottage wall, and a figure standing in it
at -3 4.2 90
select 11
verb opening
select seat 1
verb seat

echo --- the joinery, off the axis so the shared wall and the two fronts read
at -10 0 65
snap s9-bedstee

echo --- and the niche with its figure, close to
at -3 1.5 80
snap s9-statue

echo --- the balcony, from far enough out to see it is UP the trunk
at 16 -3 115
snap s9-balcony
